test_connect_options -- the options of connect, 2D and 3D (Nov 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_connect_options_tests.sh [path-to-lagrit]   20 decks, about 2 s
  open logs/summary.html

THE RULES TESTED

  connect / [delaunay] / [ifirst,ilast,istride] / [enclosing coordinates]
          and the keywords noadd, check_interface, old_order anywhere

  noadd            no points added by the interface pass or the
                   small-element pass (2D and 3D)
  check_interface  3D: also check edges between two interface points;
                   2D: a WARNING, ignored
  old_order        the insertion order of LaGriT V3.3.4 and earlier
  delaunay         token 2, the algorithm name (the only one). When it
                   is left out and token 2 is a number or pset, it is
                   taken as the start of the point range.
  enclosing        12 numbers (3D: the 4 vertices of the enclosing
  coordinates      tetrahedron) or 9 (2D: the enclosing triangle) after
                   the point range: used, with a WARNING that they are
                   deprecated. Fewer numbers: a WARNING, ignored.

  What LaGriT V3.3.4 did instead: noadd and check_interface were read
  only as the last token in 3D (so not both), noadd only as token 18
  in 2D; anything after the point range was read as 12 coordinates,
  past the end of the command if need be (no tets); a point range or
  pset in token 2 was misread (no tets, or every point connected).
  Run against V3.3.4, 11 of the 20 decks fail.

THE MESHES

  A  3D, 6 x 6 x 6 points in a unit box, two materials split by a
     tilted plane (surface / intrface): the interface pass adds points
     unless noadd
  B  3D, 5 x 5 x 5 points, pset p1 = points 1 to 60
  C  2D (triplane), 7 x 7 points, two materials split by a tilted
     plane: the interface pass adds points unless noadd

  Counts are compared with other decks of the same mesh (equal, more
  than), and only fixed where noadd fixes them (216, 125, 49 nodes), so
  the suite does not depend on how connect breaks ties.

FILES

  make_connect_options.py   writes the decks and work/expect.json
                            (what each deck tests, and what V3.3.4 did)
  check_connect_options.py  judges them; logs/summary.html
  run_connect_options_tests.sh
